 2025 Population census – May 2026 3 
Introduction 
The population census is a fundamental tool for gaining a better understanding of the demographic and 
residential characteristics of a territory. In Monaco, this statistical mission dates back to 1757 and has been 
regularly updated since then. An important milestone was reached in 2023, with the adoption of a new 
census method based on administrative sources, known as “register -based,” in place of  traditional field 
surveys. 
This methodological change, validated by the Scientific Council for Statistics and Economic Studies, the 
Government and the Prince’ s Palace, marks a major step forward: it now makes it possible to update 
demographic data on the resident population annually, improving availability and reducing operating costs. 
This 2025 report forms part of this new system and corresponds to the third year of implementation of the 
new statistical approach. It highlights the main demographic changes observed and confirms the gradual 
consolidation of this method. However, comparisons with results based on the previous  technique should 
be interpreted with caution due to the methodological break introduced in 2023. 
  
 2025 Population census – May 2026 4 
1. Evolution and main characteristics of the resident population 
1.1. Monaco’s population approaches the 39 000 mark in 2025 
Since the first census in 1757, the Principality of Monaco has undergone numerous changes, particularly 
territorial ones. These events have had an impact on the size of the population over the centuries as well as 
on the frequency of the censuses, which we re carried out every five to ten years between 1861 and 2023 , 
and annually since then. 
Figure 1. Change in the resident population from 1757 to 2025
 
 Change in calculation method  
Source: Monaco Statistics - Population censuses 
Figure 2. Change in the resident population from 2000 to 2025
 
 Change in the calculation method 
Source: Monaco Statistics - Population censuses 
As of 31 December 2025, the Principality of Monaco had 38,857 residents, 434 more than one year earlier 
(+1.1%). 
 
The population has increased by nearly 7,000 inhabitants since 2000 and has almost doubled since 1951.  
