1.5. One resident aged 18 or over in two is married
Five maritial statuses are recognised under Monegasque law:
• single: a person who has never been married;
• married: a person who is married to another person of the opposite sex;
• widowed: a person whose spouse has died;
• divorced: a person whose marriage has been dissolved by a divorce decree or agreement,
recorded in the margin of the marriage certificate and birth certificate;
• separated: a married person for whom a judgment of legal separation has been recorded in the
margin of the marriage certificate.
Table 3. Breakdown of the resident population by family situation in 2024 and 2025
Note: Percentages are calculated for the population aged 18 and over.
Source: Monaco Statistics - Population censuses
In 2025, among the 32,629 adult residents, more than half are married (16,499) and nearly a third are single
(32.5%).
Figure 8. Family situation of residents aged 18 or over by gender in 2025
Note: Percentages are calculated for the population aged 18 and over.
Source: Monaco Statistics - Population censuses
Men are proportionally more likely to be married than women (52.7% compared with 48.5%), while women
are slightly more likely to be divorced or separated and significantly more likely to be widowed.
