1.9. More than 2,700 new residents
Among the people counted in Monaco in 2025, more than 2,700, or nearly 7%, are non- Monegasque
residents aged over 18 who settled in the Principality within the last three years. The same main nationalities
(French, Italian, British, Russian, and Swiss) are represented among these “new residents.”
Figure 12. Distribution of new residents by nationality
Note: Some residents hold multiple nationalities. They are therefore counted in each community corresponding to one of their
nationalities.
Scope: Non-Monegasque aged > 18 residents who arrived between 2023 and 2025.
Sources: Police department, Monaco Statistics – Population Census 2025
Although the French community has declined the most in recent years in the Principality, the majority of
foreign residents aged over 18 who have become residents of Monaco since 2023 are French, at nearly 550
people. Italians and British each account for around 450 arrivals over the period. 190 Russians settled in the
Principality over the last three years, and nearly 1,500 new arrivals were of another nationality.
Figure 13. Distribution of residents aged 18 or over who arrived between 2023 and 2025 by sex and
nationality
Scope: Non-Monegasque aged > 18 residents who arrived between 2023 and 2025.
Sources: Police department, Monaco Statistics – Population Census 2025
