With an average age of 39.8, adult French residents who have settled since 2023 are younger than new
residents of other nationalities. By contrast, British and Swiss nationals who settled recently in the
Principality did so at an older age, with an average of 49.4.
Among the nationalities most represented among new arrivals, Russians show the largest age gap between
men and women, at 4.2 years, followed by French nationals at 2.8 years. Italians, British, and Swiss nationals
also show a gap still in favour of men, albeit to a lesser extent.
However, Analysing arrivals by nationality alone is not enough to fully reflect changes within a community .
It is also useful to consider the country of origin of new residents for a more complete picture. Indeed, while
almost all 18+ French residents who settled in Monaco since 2023 come from France (91.9%), three quarters
of British residents previously lived in the United Kingdom, less than half of Italian nationals (47.9%) are
originally from Italy, and less than a quarter of Russians come from the Russian Federation.
