1.10. More than one-third of residents are employed in Monaco
Located between French municipalities and close to the Italian border, Monaco is a major employment hub
on the Côte d’Azur. Mone gasque businesses and administrations employ more than 65,000 workers, the
vast majority of whom live outside the Principality, with nearly nine in ten not residing in Monaco.
Among working residents in Monaco, professional situations vary: employees, self -employed workers,
business owners, ect. Furthermore, these activities may be carried out in the Principality or elsewhere. Here,
only Monaco residents of working age, 18 to 64, who hold salaried jobs in the territory in 2025 are
considered.
Figure 1. Rate of salaried1 employment in Monaco among residents by age group and sector in 2025
Sources: Caisses Sociales de Monaco, Human Resources and Training Department,
Monaco Statistics – 2025 Population census
The salaried employment rate in Monaco among residents aged 18 to 64 is 35.8% in 2025, with 25.7%
working in the private sector and 10.1% in the public sector. The share of resident salaried workers is highest
among those aged 35 to 44, where more than 30% work in the private sector and nearly 15% in the public
sector, for a total of 45.5% in salaried employment.
Table 8. Rate of salaried employment in Monaco among residents by age group in 2024 and 2025
Sources: Caisses Sociales de Monaco, Human Resources and Training Department,
