 2025 Population census – May 2026 21
 Monegasque nationals
The Civil Status and Nationality Department of the Monaco City Hall updates the “sommier” (register of
Monegasque nationals), which includes information such as each person's address. Only Monegasque
nationals declaring that they reside in the Principality have been included in this database for the
census.
The family situation of Monegasques is known only for the complete population, without any details
concerning residence. Therefore, for each age/gender combination, the percentage of residents is applied
to the breakdown by family situation.
 Foreign nationals over the age of 18
The DSP issues a residence permit to any foreign national aged 16 or over wishing to stay in Monaco for
more than three months or wishing to take up residence here. To avoid double counting with the register of
schoolchildren, only foreign residents aged 18 and over holding a residence permit have been
considered in the census.
 Foreign nationals aged 3 to 17
Foreigners aged 3 -17 attending school in Monaco
The DENJS has a database of all pupils attending school in the Principality of Monaco in the public and
private sectors (under contract and not). To avoid double counting, with the residence permit register, only
resident pupils of foreign nationality aged between 3 and 17 inclusive have been included in this
database for the census.
